# Allowlist .dockerignore for the cam-worker image build context (US-001,
# CAM-177). The leading '*' excludes everything in the build context; every
# line after it is a targeted re-include for exactly what the Dockerfile
# COPYs. The workspace itself is bind-mounted at container run time (see
# docs/adr/0003-worker-isolation-boundary-dev-container.md), so nothing else
# in this repo needs to be sent to the Docker daemon on build.
#
# .devcontainer/Dockerfile performs exactly one COPY: claude-config.json ->
# /home/bun/.claude.json. If a future Dockerfile change adds a new COPY, it
# MUST come with a matching re-include line below, or the new source path
# will not exist in the build context and the build will fail.
*
!.devcontainer
.devcontainer/*
!.devcontainer/claude-config.json
